{"id":"m2://rec/open_logic/content/turing-machines/machines-computations/disciplined-machines.tex#prop:disciplined#1","source":"open_logic","snapshot":"blake3:a5eb116529d3e799289dd9f7e7530d0d446b3615f5608fe08c668241eee3c765","locator":"https://github.com/OpenLogicProject/OpenLogic/blob/1e960beff9ed7835bf3e3f1335e21af3439cd107/content/turing-machines/machines-computations/disciplined-machines.tex#L79","native_id":"content/turing-machines/machines-computations/disciplined-machines.tex#prop:disciplined","kind":"statement","text":"For every Turing machine~$M$,\nthere is a disciplined Turing machine~$M'$ which halts with output~$O$\nif $M$~halts with output~$O$, and does not halt if $M$~does not halt.\nIn particular, any function $f\\colon\\Nat^n \\to \\Nat$ computable by a\nTuring machine is also computable by a disciplined Turing machine.","class":"open","by":"textbook/1","resource":"PKGMM3P5QY","at":{"section":"85.5","kind":"prop"}}
